    {
      "filename": "The Haymarket Martyrs.jpg",
      "title": "File:The Haymarket Martyrs.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/The_Haymarket_Martyrs.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Haymarket_Martyrs.jpg",
      "width": 809,
      "height": 1035,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Unknown author",
      "description": "The Haymarket Martyrs\nThis image has faded a great deal over time, but the type face can still be read through close inspection.  The type lists each man and a respective quote, several of which were their final words quoted at their execution.  \nAdolf Fisher, \"This is the happiest moment of my life.\"\nAugust Spies, \"There will be a time when our silence will be more powerful than the voices you strangle today.\"\nAlbert R. Parsons, \"Let the Voice of the People Be Heard!\"\nLouis Lingg, \"I am an Anarchist.\"\nGeorge Engel, \"\"Hurrah For Anarchy!\"\n\nThe central type reads:\n\"MARTYRS\nFor Liberty's Cause\nNov. 11, 1887\"\n\nThe lowest type is a quote from Proudhon:\n\"For always in thine eyes, O liberty!\nShines that high light, whereby the world is saved;\n\nAnd though thou slay us, we will trust in thee.\"",
      "dateCreated": "2007-04-10 14:53:21",
      "categories": [
        "Albert Parsons",
        "Anarchists from the United States",
        "August Spies",
        "Haymarket Riot",
        "Louis Lingg",
