      "width": 2090,
      "height": 3928,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Nytasi",
      "description": "Tombstone in the Trinidad, California Cemetery. Photographed following rain that brought out more color in the stone.\nInscription reads:\n\"E. B. SCHNAUBELT\nBORN\nAPR. 5. 1855\nDIED\nMAY. 22. 1913\nMURDERED\nBY CAPITALISM\"\nThis marker inspired the book \"Murdered by Capitalism: A Memoir of 150 Years of Life and Death on the American Left\" by John Ross. \n\nEdward Bernhardt Schnaubelt was the brother of  Rudolph Schnaubelt who was accused of being the bomber from the Haymarket Riot (May 1886) in Chicago, Illinois.",
